                <pb facs="0845" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/503: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-29T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 11:28 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>125. Herrera overwhelmingly elected in a fair and quiet election. He received
                    above 225,000 votes against 6,800 for Castillo and 5,300 for Fuentes. The
                    official vote will not change these figures very materially.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
